  "swap_localisation": {
    "claim": "a detector that answers yes/no for the WHOLE base, but may be called on any target, localises its own witness: swap a candidate summand P for a class-matched base point Q and ask about R - P + Q.  No sub-base query is used anywhere (sub_base_queries = 0 on every rung).",
    "failure_modes": "Q colliding with a summand or its negative, at Theta(m/|F|) per draw, and the cell's own lambda; k independent draws take the false positives to the k-th power and the misses up by a factor k",
    "consequence": "deciding and localising are the same problem, so E3 has one free-oracle floor and not two",
